    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75537" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀσμ-άομαι</span></b> , older form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδμ-</span></b>  (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀσμή</span>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>smell
			at</i> a thing, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινος</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				541a25
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				17(2).151
			</span></i>: abs., <i>smell, have the sense of smell,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Democr.
				11
			</span></i> (in form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδμ-</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Heraclit.
				98
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>de An.</u>
				421a11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				424b16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.240
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Lucill.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ὀσμώμενα</span>”
				<i>the organs of smell,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					<u>UP</u>
					8.4
				</span></i>
			:— 
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδμᾶσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anon.
				</span></i>
			 Lond.<i><span class="en">
				33.19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>perceive, remark,</i>
			
